-----string manipulation------
->A string is a sequence of characters enclosed in single quotes (' '), double quotes (" "), or triple quotes (''' ''' or """ """)
lstrip() → L = Leftspace
rstrip() → R = Rightspace
strip() → Both sides
replace() → Change text
count() → Count occurrences
find() → Find position (-1 if not found)
index() → Find position (Error if not found)
split() → One string → Many strings (list)
join() → Many strings (list) → One string
upper() → ABC → ABC
lower() → abc → abc
len() → Number of characters
-------regular expression--------------
\s -> it matches email where there is no whitespace
\S -> meanas contain whitespace
+ -> matches one or more
\s+ -> matches one or more whitespace
@ ->matches a @ symbol without whitespace arround
\d ->matches any digit from 1 to 9
\D -> means not 1 to 9
{n}->matches exactly n occurance
{n,m}->matches the occurence between n and m
{10} ->must contain 10 digits
[]-> matches a character ,[abc]-> a || b||character
^->matches starting of the string, this not symbol ,[^abc]-> matches except a,b,character
\w->means A-Z,a-z,0-9,_
\W->means not  A-Z,a-z,0-9,_
.->matches any character (except newline)
